            "description": "Watch Borussia M'gladbach vs Borussia Dortmund highlights and goals from Bundesliga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 3, 2026. A packed house witnessed a high-stakes Bundesliga encounter as Borussia M'gladbach hosted Borussia Dortmund in a match defined by tactical discipline and technological intervention. Both sides navigated a cagey affair where the smallest of margins threatened to decide the outcome under the lights. A Tense Opening Exchange On May 3, 2026 , over 54,000 spectators filled the stands for this highly anticipated fixture, creating an electric atmosphere that belied the cautious approach taken by both managers in the opening stages. Borussia M'gladbach appeared to have found the breakthrough early in the 25th minute when Nico Elvedi found the back of the net, but the celebrations were cut short. A lengthy VAR review determined the defender was in an offside position, keeping the scoreline level. Yannik Engelhardt also went close for the hosts with a header that drifted wide, while Dortmund struggled to find their usual fluidity in the final third, leading to a stalemate as the first half drew to a close. Tactical Shifts and Rising Temperatures The second half saw an increase in physical intensity as both teams fought for control of the midfield. In the 54th minute, Kevin Stöger was cautioned for a cynical shirt-pull, followed shortly by Nico Schlotterbeck of Borussia Dortmund receiving a yellow card for a dangerous challenge. As the game entered its final quarter, Dortmund manager introduced fresh legs in the form of Fabio Silva , Salih Ozcan , and later Carney Chukwuemeka , attempting to break the deadlock. Gladbach responded with chances of their own, most notably a stinging long-range effort from Yannik Engelhardt in the 81st minute that whistled just past the upright. Late Drama and VAR Confirmation The defining moment of the match arrived in the 88th minute. Rocco Reitz showcased excellent vision to create a scoring opportunity for Haris Tabaković , who made no mistake with a clinical right-footed finish. The stadium erupted, but play was once again halted for a VAR check to verify the legitimacy of the goal. After a tense wait, the referee signaled that the goal stood in the 90th minute. Tabaković was so swept up in the emotion of the moment that he received a yellow card for his celebrations, but his contribution proved decisive. In a frantic four minutes of stoppage time, Borussia Dortmund pushed forward through Yan Couto and Daniel Svensson , but the Gladbach defense, led by timely interceptions from Joseph Scally , held firm. The final whistle confirmed a significant victory for the home side, rewarding their persistence in a match where every inch was contested."
